<header><p class="enc-kicker">Work / monument · text</p><h1 class="enc-title">Nassau Family Pact</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1783</span> · <a href="/centuries/18th-century">18th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Nassau Family Pact was a succession agreement concluded in 1783 between the branches of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/house-of-nassau">House of Nassau</a>. It provided that their lands would pass to the other branch if one line died out in the male line. When <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/william-iii-of-the-netherlands">William III of the Netherlands</a> died in 1890 leaving only a daughter, Wilhelmina, the pact gave the Grand Duchy of Luxembourg to Adolphe, the former Duke of Nassau, ending its personal union with the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kingdom-of-the-netherlands">Netherlands</a>.</p></div>
